        {
          "resource_id": "monster_action",
          "stats": {
            "action_name": {
              "value": "Thousand Ants Stance"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "(stance)\n\nThe acolyte takes the stance of thousand ants, a style mimicking the distracting strikes of a swarm of tiny, vicious creatures.\n\nThe acolyte can make thousand wounds unarmed attacks. These deal 1d12 piercing damage; are in the brawling group; and have the backstabber, forceful, and unarmed traits. While in this stance, if the acolyte successfully Trips a target, the target is flat-footed until the start of the target's next turn."
            },
